{
	"schema_version": 1,
	"description": "Inventory of every shortcut config entry on the three drivers, for PAR-41 (docs/design/one-shortcut-model.md, step 1). 'legacy_boolean' rows are a feature switch bound to one hard-coded chord; 'keyboard_slot' rows are a chord bound to a catalogue action id; 'slot_families' list the modifier prefixes under which a driver accepts any key of modifier_chords.json. 'chord.modifiers' use each driver's own modifier names. 'slot' names the keyboard slot that already binds the same chord, so a boolean and a slot never both own it after the change. Checked against the manifest, the AutoHotkey AddShortcut calls and the Lua hotkey registry by tools/test/test-shortcut-inventory-matches-sources.cjs. Updated after the macOS and Linux adoption: their slot ids and families are the role-named ones and the 18 macOS Ctrl-letter switches are keyboard slots. The Windows slots took the same ids in schema v18 and the Windows switches became slots in schema v19.",
